X.reservations=[["Reservation / Booking","Date / Time","Type","Status","Needs booking?","What to do","Recommended reserve date","Cost","Link","Notes"],["Hananosato Takadanobaba","Oct 18–25","Hotel","✅ DONE","Required","Already booked","Done","Already booked — see confirmation","","Keep booking confirmation and self-check-in instructions accessible on arrival."],["Lutia Shinjuku","Oct 20 • 11:00","Hair appointment","✅ DONE","Required","Already reserved; arrive 10–15 minutes early.","Done","~¥18,000","","Cut + straightening + treatment. Arrive 10–15 minutes early; do not move this booking casually."],["MAPPA EXPO 15th Anniversary","Oct 21 • 16:00","Timed event","✅ BOOKED","No — booked","BOOKED for two at 16:00, physical tickets NOT ISSUED. If issuance window active, try Lawson Takadanobaba Ekidori Loppi Oct 18 before hotel, otherwise Oct 19–20. Follow ticket serial/assembly directions; do not assume 16:00 arrival.","BOOKED — Sep 19, 2026","¥4,000 couple (2 × ¥2,000 General admission)","BOOKED — Overseas Lawson","BOOKED for two at 16:00, physical tickets NOT ISSUED. If issuance window active, try Lawson Takadanobaba Ekidori Loppi Oct 18 before hotel, otherwise Oct 19–20. Follow ticket serial/assembly directions; do not assume 16:00 arrival."],["Hitsumabushi Nagoya Bincho — Ikebukuro PARCO","Oct 23 • 13:30","Restaurant / hitsumabushi lunch","✅ BOOKED • 🟠 ALLERGY CONTACT PENDING","No","BOOKED 13:30 Oct23 for 2. Restaurant allergen/cross-contact contact still pending; do not assume safe without confirmation.","BOOKED — Sep 12, 2026","~¥8,000–10,000 couple planning range","BOOKED via EBICA","BOOKED 13:30 Oct23 for 2. Restaurant allergen/cross-contact contact still pending; do not assume safe without confirmation."],["Nihon Minka-en / Japan Open-Air Folk House Museum","Oct 23 • 09:30–11:30 FULL TWO HOURS at Nihon Minka-en; no booking needed","Open-air museum / old-Japan experience","🟢 NO RESERVATION NEEDED","No","Enter via Minka-en FRONT/EAST Gate at 09:30 after Masugata Tenjinsha shrine (or direct from station if delayed), EXIT front gate at 11:30 to preserve full 2h AND reach Odakyu Mukogaoka-Yuen platform before ⭐12:08 Shinjuku express. Confirm on the day; 12:28 backup creates tighter Bincho 13:30 arrival. Oct23 Yamato ticket EMERGENCY: collect from 08:00 if READY, skip shrine, prioritize paid musical.","Oct 23 — day of","¥1,100 couple (¥550/adult)","INFO — Nihon Minka-en","No reservation required. Protected stop; current October hours 09:30–17:00, last admission 16:30."],["SPY×FAMILY 2 Musical","Oct 23 • 17:45","Physical tickets","🟠 PAID — SHIPPING / PICKUP PENDING","Already bought","PAID, physical tickets shipping/pickup still pending. Oct20 Yamato pickup if READY, Oct21 backup; if emergency pickup Oct23, SKIP Masugata shrine to protect the show.","Already purchased • ship target Oct 19 • pickup target Oct 20 ~08:00","¥22,000 PAID — excluded from remaining trip budget","","PAID, physical tickets shipping/pickup still pending. Oct20 Yamato pickup if READY, Oct21 backup; if emergency pickup Oct23, SKIP Masugata shrine to protect the show."],["Miyanoen Sayama Tea-Picking","Oct 24 • 10:00","Experience","✅ BOOKED","No — booked","BOOKED 10:00 Oct24 for two; chamusume outfits confirmed, 2026 fee TBD, official ~90 minutes plus changing. Check weather-cancellation messages.","BOOKED — Sep 17, 2026","¥4,000+ couple; chamusume outfit fee TBD","BOOKED via email — Miyanoen","BOOKED 10:00 Oct24 for two; chamusume outfits confirmed, 2026 fee TBD, official ~90 minutes plus changing. Check weather-cancellation messages."],["Edo-Tokyo Open Air Architectural Museum","Oct 21 • ~11:35–13:25/13:35 museum exit target","Museum / historic architecture","🟢 NO ADVANCE RESERVATION REQUIRED","No — designated-date advance ticket optional","Museum admission on arrival. Protect museum exploration; safer plan is depart museum ~13:25–13:35 for MAPPA 16:00 (13:45 only if live route meets ticket assembly). Kokubunji historic-area micro-stop optional, skip to protect transfer. Kura lunch only if allergy safe; bring known-safe food backup.","Oct 21 — same day is fine","¥800 couple (¥400/adult)","INFO — official museum","Moved from Oct 24 to Oct 21. October hours 09:30–16:30, last admission 16:00. Same-day tickets are available. Tokyo Grand Tea Ceremony is no longer part of the fixed itinerary."],["N’EX TOKYO Round Trip + Reserved Seats","Oct 18 arrival + Oct 25 early Narita transfer","Transport / reserved seats","🟡 TO BUY / RESERVE • NOT YET BOOKED","Yes for preferred direct trains","Buy N’EX TOKYO Round Trip Ticket and reserve 2 seats for arrival N’EX 50 plus Oct 25 N’EX 9 Shinjuku→NRT T2・3.","NOW","¥10,400 couple (¥5,200/adult round trip)","BOOK — JR EAST / N’EX","14-day validity covers Oct 18→Oct 25. Arrival target N’EX 50 19:53→21:18. Oct 25 target N’EX 9: Shinjuku 08:05→NRT T2・3 09:25, chosen to catch Toyoko’s 09:55 T2→hotel shuttle."],["Enoden Suica pay-as-you-go (3 rides; no day pass)","Oct 19","Transport","🟢 SUICA PAY-AS-YOU-GO • NO PASS NEEDED","No reservation","Tap Suica on each of 3 planned Enoden rides: Kamakura→Hase; Gokurakuji→Inamuragasaki; Inamuragasaki→Koshigoe. No advance purchase.","Oct 19 — day of","~¥1,280 couple total; verify station fares on the day","INFO — Noriorikun","Suica pay-as-you-go for three rides: no Enoden day pass under this route."],["Odakyu Romancecar Enoshima No. 6","Oct 19 • 19:39 Katase-Enoshima → 20:48 Shinjuku","Transport / reserved-seat limited express","🟡 OPTIONAL • BUY ON DAY IF 2 SEATS AVAILABLE","Optional; unbooked; regular Odakyu via Fujisawa backup","Check Odakyu timetable and same-day availability for 2 seats. Buy limited-express tickets only if available; otherwise regular Odakyu via Fujisawa. Do not mark booked.","Oct 19 — same-day if available","Ticketless limited-express surcharge ¥1,400 couple + base IC fare ~¥1,298 couple","BOOK — Romancecar","UNBOOKED OPTIONAL 19:39–20:48 direct train only if two same-day seats are available. Otherwise regular Odakyu via Fujisawa."],["Tokyo Hyakki Yako 2026 + Day 7 Sayama→Koenji transfer","Oct 24 • parade 14:30 • finale 15:25–15:50","Free spectator event + transport","🟢 VIEWING FREE / NO RESERVATION","No for spectators","Miyanoen booked 10:00 x2; official experience ~90min plus changes, prefer 12:03 Sayamadai-minami SAT bus→Sayamashi ~12:10 then ⭐12:26 Seibu Express→Takadanobaba ~13:14→JR via Shinjuku LOCAL Koenji SOUTH EXIT / Look parade 14:30. 12:22 bus connects to 12:46 Express→13:34 and may reach LOOK only around 14:30; skip lunch. 12:42 bus high-risk; no guarantee of parade opening. Spectators free/no registration.","Oct 24 — day of","¥0 event viewing; local fares in Day 7 transport budget","INFO — official Koenji Fest","Oct24 Koenji Fest OFFICIAL https://koenjifes.jp/2026/hyakkiyako/ confirms 14:30 LOOK SOUTH procession, finale15:25–15:50; separate North Exit stage https://koenjifes.jp/2026/north_square/ has Tokyo Hyakki Yako 15:25–15:40. Free viewers, no booking. Arrival crucial: Miyanoen ~11:30 finish + changing, ⭐12:03 bus 狭山台南→Sayamashi and ⭐12:26 Seibu express→Takadanobaba13:14; late 12:22 bus+12:46 express jeopardizes procession. IF BOTH procession+stage missed/cancelled, SKIP Koenji detour, head directly via Shinjuku/Odakyu Shimokitazawa; optional Kitazawa Hachimangu shrine 12min walk, or Hanegi Park local→Umegaoka before Oct24 16:55 sunset. See If We Have Time tab; fixed bookings unchanged."],["Restaurant Kura — Edo-Tokyo Open Air Architectural Museum","Oct 21 • ~12:30","Museum lunch / udon","🟢 WALK-IN","No reservation","Walk-in museum lunch only if seafood/shrimp/crab allergy and cross-contact safety can be confirmed. Bring a known-safe backup meal/snack; never rely on unverified udon broth. Aim ~12:30–13:00, but adjust to actual museum arrival.","Oct 21 — walk in","~¥1,500–2,500 couple","INFO — official museum café page","Kura museum lunch ~12:30 only if severe shrimp/crab/seafood allergy AND cross-contact safety confirmed by staff; never assume broth safe. Carry known-safe meal/snack backup. ¥1,500–2,500 is meal allowance for Kura OR safe alternative; if museum entry delayed, shorten lunch or use backup without rushing."],["Bar Lupin","Oct 21 • ~19:15","Bar / BSD pilgrimage","🟢 WALK-IN","No","Walk in after CHA・GINZA + Kiya knife shopping.","Oct 21 — walk in","~¥6,000–10,000 couple","","Bar Lupin BSD visit: walk-in/cash-only reported, cover charge reported; queue and dinner menu uncertain. Do not rely on it as only meal. Confirm ingredients/cross-contact or eat known-safe alternative. Budget ¥6,000–10,000 includes bar/alternative dinner planning, not guaranteed cost."],["Dr.STONE PARTY vol.2 — NATSLIVE CAFE Omotesando","Oct 20 • 14:50–16:00 CONFIRMED","Collaboration café / anime event","✅ BOOKED","REQUIRED — all dates reservation-only","BOOKED Oct20 at 14:50 for two. Reserved ¥7,700 menu is unpaid. Private booking reference stays off the public app.","DONE — Sep 11, 2026","¥7,700 reserved menu couple — NOT YET PAID • merch additional/TBD","RESERVE — Dr.STONE PARTY vol.2","BOOKED Oct20 at 14:50 for two. Reserved ¥7,700 menu is unpaid. Private booking reference stays off the public app."],["夜のケーキ屋さん®️歌舞伎町 — Custom Cake","PICKUP DATE UNDECIDED — no date scheduled","Custom cake / preorder","🟡 DECIDE NOW — ORDER OR REMOVE","Required for custom design","OPTIONAL IDEA ONLY. NOT ORDERED, NO PICKUP DATE, NOT in any fixed itinerary or 15-min schedule. Reconsider only after confirmation/payment.","NOW","~¥5,000–7,000 planning range","ORDER — official LINE","OPTIONAL IDEA ONLY. NOT ORDERED, NO PICKUP DATE, NOT in any fixed itinerary or 15-min schedule. Reconsider only after confirmation/payment."],["Toyoko Inn Narita Airport Honkan","Oct 25–26 • 1 night","Airport hotel","✅ BOOKED / PAID • 🟠 BAG DROP CONFIRM PENDING","No — booked","Hotel Oct25–26 PAID. Written early luggage-drop confirmation still pending; do not promise baggage storage.","DONE — Oct 4, 2026","PAID — excluded from remaining trip budget","BOOKED via Agoda","Hotel Oct25–26 PAID. Written early luggage-drop confirmation still pending; do not promise baggage storage."]];X.budget=[["💰 JAPAN TRIP BUDGET – COUPLE","Budget","Main spending breakdown"],["Day 1 – Arrival + N'EX","¥30,000  |  ≈ ₱12,000","N’EX TOKYO Round Trip tickets ¥10,400 couple (Oct 18 arrival + Oct 25 airport-hotel transfer) + dinner/snacks + local transport/arrival expenses → safe Day 1 cap remains ~¥30,000."],["Day 2 – Kamakura + Enoshima","¥45,000  |  ≈ ₱18,000","Kamakura/Enoshima transport + Enoden Suica fares estimated ¥1,280 for two over 3 rides (¥220+¥200+¥220 per adult; cheaper than ¥1,600 couple day passes) + Kosokuji ~¥100 each + optional unbooked Romancecar surcharge + attractions + meals. Seafood lunch no longer default; verify allergy-safe venue. Day 2 cap ¥45,000 unchanged."],["Day 3 – Lutia + 100-Yen + Dr.STONE + Shibuya + Donki","¥225,000  |  ≈ ₱90,000","MORNING CHOICE: Yamato 08:00 if READY + Can★Do, OR Tetsugakudo Park 08:00–08:45 (replaces Yamato/Can★Do). Lutia ¥18,000; NATSLIVE reserved menu ¥7,700 unpaid; SHIBUYA109 ¥30,000 protected 17:55–20:45; Martin shoes ¥70,000 reserve; Donki ¥50,000; meals and transport. Café/dinner allergy checks outstanding. Donki 21:30–22:30, hotel ~23:00–23:30. Day 3 planning range ¥192,700–209,000, excluding undecided cake; keep ¥225,000 safe cap."],["Day 4 – Kokubunji + Edo-Tokyo Museum + MAPPA + Ginza","¥129,000  |  ≈ ₱51,600","Day 4 ¥129,000 conservative cap UNCHANGED. Itemized couple estimate ¥49,300–87,800, arithmetically verified: breakfast ¥2,000–3,000; rail/bus ¥3,500–5,000; Tonogayato+Otaka ¥500; museum ¥800; Kura lunch or verified allergy-safe substitute ¥1,500–2,500; knife ¥20,000–35,000; snack/drink ¥0–2,000; MAPPA merch ¥10,000–20,000; tea ¥2,000–4,000; Bar Lupin/drinks or safe alternative dinner ¥6,000–10,000; contingency ¥3,000–5,000. MAPPA admission ¥4,000 ALREADY PAID, excluded. Safer route: leave Kokubunji historic area by ~10:35 (optional micro-stop); museum exit ~13:25–13:35, ~80–100 min travel to MAPPA, obey printed ticket assembly instructions. Kura and Bar Lupin food NOT allergy-cleared; carry known-safe food backup. Oct 18 Lawson pickup planned, not yet collected. Actual rail/bus fares and shopping prices subject to day-of verification."],["Day 5 – Yokohama + BSD Pilgrimage + Animate","¥40,000  |  ≈ ₱16,000","¥40,000 Day 5 cap unchanged; ¥19,600–35,600 estimated couple. Added Harbor View Park rose garden (same park as museum), Motomachi Park/Bluff No.80 ruins, Itsukushima Shrine; Yato Bridge optional. Protected BSD museum, Agency-inspired Information Culture Center exterior, Osanbashi International Passenger Terminal ROOFTOP, sunset, Animate. Transport JR Yamanote outer loop→Shinagawa→Keihin-Tohoku/Negishi→Ishikawacho; walking route Yamate→Motomachi→Nihon-odori→harbor→Noge; JR Sakuragicho→Yokohama→VIVRE, return via Shinjuku or Shinagawa. No new ticketed attractions; taxi extra."],["Day 6 – Masugata Tenjinsha + Minka-en (full 2h) + Bincho + Ikebukuro Keyboards + SPY×FAMILY 2","¥150,000  |  ≈ ₱60,000","SPY tickets already PAID/excluded + Masugata Tenjinsha FREE (optional offertory) + Nihon Minka-en entrance ¥1,100/couple + Bincho 13:30 ✅ BOOKED (~¥8k–10k/couple) + ¥80k reserve for two prebuilt keyboards + accessories + theater merch + meals/transport. Earlier ⭐07:46 Shinjuku→Mukogaoka and ⭐12:08 return, museum 09:30–11:30 FULL 2h. Gotokuji moved to If We Have Time, NOT DAY6. Cap unchanged ¥150k."],["Day 7 – Sayama Tea + Koenji Yokai Parade + Direct Shimokitazawa","¥25,000  |  ≈ ₱10,000","MAIN: Miyanoen 10:00 BOOKED for two with chamusume outfits confirmed (2026 rental fee TBD), official ~90min + changing. SAT Seibu Takadanobaba 07:35→Sayamashi08:20, bus 08:49 East Exit stand2; return ⭐12:03 bus from 狭山台南 then ⭐12:26 Sayamashi EXPRESS→Takadanobaba13:14 (12:22 bus/12:46 train backup risks parade). Koenji LOOK 14:30–15:50 free spectator; North Exit stage 15:25–15:40. After parade DIRECT Shimokitazawa vintage, ~17:00–20:30 target; Mabashi Inari optional but loses shopping. IF Miyanoen cancels: Ogikubo Three Gardens nature alternative (Otaguro/Kadokawa free, Tekigaiso historic interior ~¥300/adult optional; tea/activity fee not spent). IF parade missed: closest low-cost Shimokitazawa alternatives Kitazawa Hachimangu FREE (optional goshuin purchase ¥500–1,000) or Hanegi Park FREE (Odakyu LOCAL return fare additional), choose ONE only before 16:55 sunset; can also skip all and shop earlier. Main couple Day7 operating CAP remains ¥25,000 (≈₱10,000) and clothing purchases variable/outside operating cap; optional train/goshuin spending must come out of existing food/contingency, NO new overall trip-budget increase; Kichijoji not on fixed route."],["Day 8 – Early Narita + Toyoko Bag Drop + Naritasan Nature","¥40,000  |  ≈ ₱16,000","DAY8 ITEMIZED COUPLE ESTIMATE now ¥29,960–38,960 (see Budget rows 19–36), compared with unchanged ¥40,000 day cap. Details: Keisei Main Line airport T2↔Keisei Narita 2 people return ¥1,120 (¥280×4); local JR Takadanobaba→Shinjuku planning allowance ¥400; NEW Naritasan Museum of Calligraphy Oct20 admission ¥800×2=¥1,600; Fudō no Ōido garden, 2026 chrysanthemum show, waterfall/ponds/Ukimidō/suikinkutsu ¥0; TWO STANDARD 30ml primaniacs fragrances ¥7,920×2=¥15,840; lunch ¥4–6k, dinner ¥3–5k, breakfast/drinks/snacks ¥1–2k, optional local crafts/wagashi ¥1–3k, contingency ¥2–4k. Price/stock of different-size specialty perfumes may exceed ¥7,920. Toyoko Honkan ALREADY PAID excluded. N’EX TOKYO RT ¥10,400 COUPLE budgeted on Day1 ONLY (Oct18 + Oct25), not twice; N’EX tickets and reserved seats still pending. Existing Suica load/cash withdrawal are funding allocations, not new costs. Overall trip cap stays ¥703,500; no additional Day8 spending required for new Narita hidden gems."],["Day 9 – Departure via Cebu","¥12,000  |  ≈ ₱4,800","Toyoko→NRT shuttle ¥0 + airport breakfast/meal + longer Cebu connection meal/snacks + small final contingency. No N’EX. Latest flight schedule: 5J 5063 NRT T2 08:55→CEB T2 13:15, then 5J 4084 CEB T1 19:35→ILO 20:30. Day 9 cap remains sufficient."],["✈️ Cebu Pacific additional baggage","¥7,500  |  ≈ ₱3,000","Additional checked-baggage allowance / upgrade reserve with Cebu Pacific → max ₱3,000 planning reserve. IMPORTANT: verify both BAGGAGE PIECE COUNT and total weight for the two keyboard boxes + shopping; adding kilograms does not automatically mean another checked piece. Kiya knife must travel securely in checked baggage."],["TOTAL TRIP BUDGET","¥703,500  |  ≈ ₱281,400","Verified October 14: 9 day caps total ¥696,000 and Cebu extra baggage reserve ¥7,500, giving full trip safe cap ¥703,500 (≈₱281,400 at ¥1≈₱0.40). Day 8 hidden gems and museum already included in its ¥40,000 cap. Estimated Day8 couple allocation ¥29,960–38,960 (≈₱11,984–15,584); details in Budget A19:D36. N’EX return ticket is part of Day1 ¥10,400 couple roundtrip allocation only. Toyoko already paid/excluded. Physical cash and Suica are payment methods, not extra trip costs."],["💴 Physical cash to withdraw","¥88,000  |  ≈ ₱35,200",""],["📱 Suica – Cha","¥15,000  |  ≈ ₱6,000",""],["📱 Suica – Martin","¥15,000  |  ≈ ₱6,000",""],["📱 Suica total","¥30,000  |  ≈ ₱12,000",""],["🧾 DAY 8 RECALCULATED COST — 2 ADULTS (DETAILS INCLUDED IN ¥40,000 DAY CAP)","Narita hidden-gem route · 25 Oct 2026","All values in JPY. This section is a breakdown of Day 8 row 10, NOT an added budget."]];X.day8Breakdown=[["Cost category (Day 8)","LOW estimate ¥","HIGH estimate ¥","Assumptions / source / no double count"],["Keisei Main Line T2 ⇄ Keisei Narita, 2 adults","¥1,120","¥1,120","¥280 adult each way × 2 people × 2 rides; 2026 published single-ticket fare, subject to day-of fare. Suica debit, not an additional Suica top-up."],["JR local Takadanobaba → Shinjuku, 2 adults","¥400","¥400","Planning allowance ¥200/person, not an exact 2026 confirmed IC fare; charge from Suica. N’EX long-distance leg separately counted Day 1."],["Naritasan Museum of Calligraphy — 2 adults","¥1,600","¥1,600","Official October 20, 2026 revised admission ¥800/adult, last admission 15:30; 2 × ¥800. This is the only fixed new paid attraction."],["Fudō no Ōido + chrysanthemums + Shinshoji + park gems","¥0","¥0","Sacred garden, 2026 Oct20–Nov15 chrysanthemums, waterfall/ponds/Ukimidō and suikinkutsu free with public access; optional offerings not included."],["primaniacs 30ml STANDARD character fragrances × 2","¥15,840","¥15,840","Official standard ¥7,920 tax included ×2; price and stock vary by specific character/size, e.g. 100ml and sets may be costlier. Plan exactly TWO standard fragrances."],["Narita lunch for 2","¥4,000","¥6,000","Restaurant NOT booked, allergy-safe meal. Budget ~¥2,000–3,000 per person, or less for quick meal if needed."],["Dinner for 2 near Toyoko / Narita airport","¥3,000","¥5,000","Allow ~¥1,500–2,500 per person, varies by availability and allergies; keep Oct26 early wake."],["Breakfast, drinks, snacks for 2","¥1,000","¥2,000","Early Tokyo breakfast + afternoon drinks + next-morning packaged breakfast/snack. No hotel breakfast assumption before Oct26 shuttle."],["Optional Japanese crafts / wagashi souvenirs","¥1,000","¥3,000","Fujikura Shoten or sweets ONLY if desired; optional Yōkan Museum/Tourist Pavilion free. Reduce this item if you choose 100ml fragrance."],["General contingency","¥2,000","¥4,000","Small unexpected rail variation, food cost, lockers or convenience. Taxi, large specialty perfumes and extra luggage purchases outside estimate."],["ESTIMATED DAY 8 SPENDING — COUPLE","¥29,960","¥38,960","DAY 8 itemized range: ¥29,960–38,960 = approximately ₱11,984–15,584 at existing ¥1≈₱0.40 planning rate. Includes ¥2,000–4,000 contingency allowance and is NOT additional to Budget row 10."],["EXISTING DAY 8 OPERATING CAP","¥40,000","¥40,000","Same ¥40,000 cap from Budget row 10; hotels prepaid/excluded."],["UNSPENT ROOM UNDER CAP","¥10,040","¥1,040","LOW spend leaves more cushion; HIGH spend leaves less. Higher-value perfume or souvenir purchases may exceed cap."],["IMPORTANT: N’EX TOKYO ROUND TRIP ¥10,400 COUPLE","COUNTED IN DAY 1 ONLY","NOT IN DAY 8 AGAIN","Oct18 inbound and Oct25 return are one round-trip ticket; ticket still unpurchased / seat reservation pending."],["TOTAL TRIP CAP and IC CARD NOTE","¥703,500 UNCHANGED","SUICA LOADING IS FUNDING","Existing ¥30,000 two-card Suica load and ¥88,000 cash withdrawal are payment allocations, NOT extra costs on top of the daily budgets."],["PRICE/ROUTE QA NOTE","Standard fragrance ¥7,920 ×2","Keisei ticket ~¥280 adult/ride","Official Naritasan Museum admission changes to ¥800/adult Oct20, 2026. Verify actual selected primaniacs items and fare before buying."]];
